## 📖 1. Project Overview & Vision

### The Problem
Traditional 2D productivity apps (flat calendars, text-heavy Kanban boards, and ticking 25-minute Pomodoro timers) consistently fail neurodivergent children (ADHD, Autism, and AuDHD) for four clinical reasons:
1. **Executive Dysfunction & Working Memory Overload:** Flat lists of text blend together, triggering choice paralysis ("blank-page freeze") and out-of-sight, out-of-mind forgetfulness.
2. **ADHD Time Blindness (Barkley, 1997):** Abstract digital countdown numbers (`04:59... 04:58`) do not register urgency in the ADHD prefrontal cortex until it is too late, while fast-ticking clocks induce anxiety in autistic learners.
3. **Sensory & Emotional Dysregulation During Transitions:** Children cannot initiate homework or daily routines while their nervous system is hyper-aroused (fidgety, overwhelmed by school transit) or hypo-aroused (brain fog).
4. **Interoceptive Blindness:** Neurodivergent learners frequently miss internal thirst and hunger cues until dehydration or low blood sugar triggers a meltdown or focus crash.

### Our Solution: The "Anchor-and-Release" Spatial Bridge
**LumaDesk VR** is not a 12-hour virtual prison—it is a **3-to-15 minute Spatial Transition & Focus Cockpit** built around a three-table physical layout:
* **360° VR Sanctuary Mode (Nervous System Reset & Rehearsal):** Children step into a calm 360° environment (`Forest`, `Ocean`, `Dino`, or `Space`) for 90 seconds to regulate their breathing, clear mental clutter, and pre-rehearse upcoming daily transitions (`☀️ Morning`, `🚌 Commute`, `📚 Study`, `🌙 Night`).
* **Mixed Reality Passthrough Mode (`🏠 Real Room (MR)`):** When it is time to do real-world homework on paper, tapping **Real Room (MR)** hides the virtual sky dome and hollows out the center desk surface—allowing the child to see their physical notebook and pencil through the headset while their **3D Shrinking Focus Timer Ring**, **Left-Wing 3D Kanban Board**, **Luma Study Companion**, and **Wit.ai Voice Orb** float right around their real desk.

